<style>
  @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Serif+Display:ital@0;1&family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap");

  .faq-section {
    padding: 3rem 0;
    background-color: var(--tg-section-background); /* secondary/surface */
    font-family: var(--tg-body-font-family);
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .faq-section {
      padding: 4rem 0;
    }
  }
  .faq-container {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .faq-container {
      padding: 0 2rem;
    }
  }
  .faq-header {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto 4rem auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .faq-subtitle {
    color: var(--tg-primary-color);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .faq-title {
    font-family: var(--tg-heading-font-family);
    color: var(--tg-heading-font-color);
    font-size: 1.875rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .faq-title {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
  }

  .faq-wrapper {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  /* Keep basic styling similar to Accordion component from React */
  .faq-item {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #e1e4eb;
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--tg-heading-font-color);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color 0.3s ease;
    list-style: none; /* Hide default marker */
  }
  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-item summary:hover {
    color: var(--tg-primary-color);
  }

  .faq-icon {
    width: 1.25rem;
    height: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--tg-heading-font-color);
    transition:
      transform 0.3s ease,
      color 0.3s ease;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .faq-item summary:hover .faq-icon {
    color: var(--tg-primary-color);
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }
  .faq-item[open] {
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px -4px rgba(24, 32, 78, 0.08); /* shadow-card */
  }

  .faq-content {
    padding: 0 1.5rem 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    color: var(--tg-paragraph-color);
    line-height: 1.625;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>

<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="faq-container">
    <div class="faq-header">
      <span class="faq-subtitle">FAQs</span>
      <h2 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-wrapper">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          Is the Social Stock Exchange in India regulated by SEBI?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          Yes. The Social Stock Exchange segment on NSE/BSE operates under
          SEBI's SSE framework, with eligibility criteria, listing guidelines,
          continuous disclosure and social audit norms.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          What is a ZCZP bond on SSE?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          ZCZP stands for Zero Coupon Zero Principal. It is a Social Stock
          Exchange India instrument where you get no interest and no principal
          back. The entire amount is treated as an impact contribution, with
          audited impact reporting and potential Section 80G tax benefits.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          What is the minimum and maximum I can invest?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          The minimum investment for many ZCZP issues is now ₹1,000, especially
          for retail investors. Larger allocations up to and beyond ₹10,00,000
          are possible for high-value individuals, companies and institutions
          (Category III or higher).
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          Is ZCZP impact investing profitable in India?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          Financially, no. ZCZP instruments are designed as donation-like impact
          tools, not for financial returns. The "return" is measurable social
          change, plus Income Tax benefits via Section 80G where applicable.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          Can my company use this for CSR?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          Not at present.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          Can NGOs or investors get free help on SSE?
          <svg
            class="faq-icon"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
            width="24"
            height="24"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path>
          </svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq-content">
          DR Associates offers free SSE resources, FAQs and webinars, plus a
          free 30-minute consultation if you want to discuss listing, compliance
          or impact investing via Social Stock Exchange India.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
